.el .ds Aq '
.TH garuda-toolbox-queue 1  "garuda-toolbox 6.3.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-queue \- Queue changes as the window does, then apply them as one plan. While the window runs, its own queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox queue\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queue changes as the window does, then apply them as one plan. While the window runs, its own queue
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text, for scripts
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-queue\-show(1)
Show the queued changes, numbered, and the plan that carries them out
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-queue\-add(1)
Queue a change instead of carrying it out now. Type the change as its own command
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-queue\-remove(1)
Take back one queued change, by its number in `queue show` or by its name
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-queue\-clear(1)
Take back every queued change
.TP
garuda\-toolbox\-queue\-apply(1)
Carry out the whole queue as one plan, with one password
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox queue add apps install firefox
  garuda\-toolbox queue
  garuda\-toolbox queue apply
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox(1)
